* '''Typhoon No. 3''' passes [[Okaiken]] — the [[Kagami Mountains]] shred the storm's circulation, downgrading it to a tropical storm; no fatalities, 14 minor injuries; 48,000 of 64,000 households restored; evacuees returning home.
* The '''[[Okaiken International Cooperation Agency|OICA]]''' school funds scandal in '''[[Dagit]]''' — ¥4.1B of ¥6.8B allocated for school construction missing; no schools built; funds routed to entities controlled by Dagit Minister of Infrastructure [[Enrique Magalona|Magalona]] and associates; Sadanuma: "We didn't vote for you to spend Okaiken money on useless stadiums."
* Targeted attacks on '''[[Ayorin]]'''-owned businesses in [[Toyozawa]] and Okami — windows smashed, graffiti "We don't want people like you here"; [[TMPD]] investigating connections to organised [[masugu]] ultra groups; 12,000-strong Ayorin community on edge.
* The Baliscan '''[[Secretariat of Climate and the Environment (Balisca)|Secretariat of Climate and the Environment]]''' launches investigation into [[Toyozawa bulky waste incident|Sanese waste exports after Toyozawa incident]].
* [[Pasundan]] restrict the movement of Cannabis coming from [[Terangon]] following the recent change of Cannabis Legality act by president [[Anang Setiadji]].

